    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Goal\nImplement the Import as workspace onboarding flow using the shared validation and Git-preparation APIs. Reuse the project import preparation modal and progress UI where possible, extending them to show multiple repositories.\n\n## Scope\n- Call POST /imports/validate after a user selects a folder with importKind: workspace.\n- Block downstream onboarding until validation completes.\n- Show blocking errors before harness selection.\n- Render the selected root separately from child repositories.\n- Group child repositories by ready, needs Git initialization, needs commit, needs remote, and blocked states.\n- Show a reusable Git preparation modal with the workspace context, affected repository list, per-repository required actions, editable remotes, Back, and Continue.\n- Let the user review and approve only the repositories and actions that will be changed.\n- Call POST /imports/prepare-git after approval and render GitPreparationEvent progress for every repository and step.\n- Show partial success and failure clearly, with retry/back recovery.\n\n## UX Requirements\n- Never show workspace or orchestrator creation options before validation passes.\n- Do not present raw internal error codes to users.\n- Make the scope of every Git mutation explicit before execution.\n- Reuse the project import modal and progress primitives, but add the multi-repository grouping and approval UI required for workspace mode.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- A workspace with ready child repositories can continue without Git preparation.\n- A workspace with partially initialized children displays only each child's missing steps.\n- A non-Git child displays git_init, git_commit, and set_remote.\n- The root repository status and child repository statuses are visibly distinct.\n- Each repository's progress is visible during preparation.\n- If a child fails, the UI explains which repository and step failed and provides recovery actions.\n- Component tests cover ready workspace, partial child setup, non-Git child, validation failure, multi-repo progress, and partial preparation failure.\n\n## Dependencies\n- [#4757](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/4757)\n- Reuse the project UI work in [#4756](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/4756).\n\n## Related\n- [#3686](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/3686)",
